---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const contact = `mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Privacy request')}`;
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow prose">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p>Able Bodied (“we,” “us,” or “our”) is a nonprofit organization dedicated to helping people around the world connect and experience “able bodied” adventures. We value your privacy, especially that of the children and families we serve.</p>

      <h2>1. How we collect information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Directly from you:</strong> when you apply for a program, make a donation, or contact us.</li>
        <li><strong>From parents and guardians:</strong> we collect information about riders under 13 only when a parent or legal guardian provides it during registration.</li>
        <li><strong>This website:</strong> the site sets no cookies and uses no tracking or advertising tools. Forms and calendars we link to (Google Forms and Google Calendar) are run by Google under its own privacy policy.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Identifying information:</strong> name, email and contact details.</li>
        <li><strong>Rider information:</strong> for program safety and eligibility, we may collect age, physical requirements and equipment needs.</li>
        <li><strong>Financial information:</strong> processed by secure third-party payment services for donations or fees. We never see your full card details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>In accordance with COPPA, we do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children under 13.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Parental consent:</strong> all information about a minor must be submitted by a parent or guardian. By submitting an application for a rider under 13, you confirm that you are the legal guardian and consent to our processing of this information.</li>
        <li><strong>Data minimization:</strong> we only collect the information a child needs to take part in Able Bodied programs.</li>
        <li><strong>Parental rights:</strong> parents may review their child’s information, ask us to delete it, or refuse further collection by <a href={contact}>contacting us</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How we use and share information</h2>
      <p>We use this information to run our programs and coordinate events.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Sharing:</strong> we may share information with program instructors or vetted volunteers as needed for safety.</li>
        <li><strong>No sale of data:</strong> we do not sell or rent personal information to anyone.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Security</h2>
      <p>We maintain reasonable administrative and technical safeguards, such as encryption and access limits, to protect the information of our riders and donors.</p>

      <h2>6. Contact us</h2>
      <p>To ask for access to, or deletion of, your (or your child’s) information, contact:</p>
      <p>
        {SITE.mailingAddress.map((l) => <>{l}<br /></>)}
        <a href={contact}>{SITE.email}</a><br />
        408-890-SKIN
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
